From 7c3e123dc4aab49fd969ffd35a6d0f390f802612 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 12:12:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Square bullet markers, transparent Pile-On ad briefs,
 less-rounded Pre-Call-Read, proper dropdown for the Trend metric picker
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- simple-markdown.tsx: report bullet lists now use a small colored
  square marker (matching Show Rate Setup's SquareLabel convention)
  instead of the default round list-disc dot.

- pile-on-ad-creative-briefs.tsx: this is a separate file from Show
  Rate Setup's own ad-briefs accordion (which was already transparent)
  and had been missed in the earlier surface-glass sweep — every
  no-ambient-glow/surface-glass instance plus two explicit bg-zinc
  fills swapped for bg-transparent + border. Its page
  (skills/pile-on/page.tsx) also had no bg-dot-grid wrapper at all,
  unlike every other skill page — added.

- pre-call-read-pipeline.tsx: every rounded-2xl -> rounded-lg and
  rounded-xl -> rounded-md across the toolbar and panels, matching the
  "less rounded" ask. (Investigated the reported month-switching bug
  here too — unlike the earlier Leak Map bug, this file's fetch is
  already scoped by month and selectedEntryId already resets via a
  selectedDayEntries-based effect; nothing structurally wrong surfaced
  from a static read. Flagged back to the user for a more specific
  repro rather than guessed at further.)

- leak-map-trend-chart.tsx: replaced the native <select> metric picker
  with ActionMenu/ActionMenuItem, the same dropdown component used
  throughout the rest of the app (e.g. leak-map-schedule.tsx's audit
  picker), instead of an unstyled generic browser control.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AkznvRLnBokzbdmJ2WwaEM
